# scripts/what_the_commit_gate_actually_costs_over_time_2026-11-08.py, reading
# .cdsfl_tmp/precommit_durations.jsonl. It reports 5 full boards, mean 706.00 s
# (11.77 min), sd 35.64, 95 per cent t-interval [661.75, 750.25], and EXCLUDES 1
# short run of 12 s at exit 1 by naming it rather than averaging an
# infrastructure refusal into the cost of a board. The 104 files were measured
# at 1,271 tests in 890.45 s, so the gate becomes about 1,596.45 s = 26.61 min.
#
# ★ THE CONTRADICTION, STATED PLAINLY RATHER THAN LEFT FOR A READER TO FIND.
# The header above says a per-commit gate costing 11 minutes would be bypassed
# within a day, and that a guard which gets bypassed is not a guard. At a mean
